"osc.host": "IP address",
"osc.howto.eos": "1. On the console: Setup → System Settings → Show Control → OSC.\n2. Turn on OSC RX, set OSC UDP RX Port = 8000.\n3. For the check: OSC TX on, OSC UDP TX IP = this Mac's IP (below), TX Port = 8001.\n4. Enter the console's IP here (Setup → Network on the console).",
"osc.howto.generic": "1. In the program or device, find the OSC settings and switch on OSC input.\n2. Note its IP and port and enter them here.\n3. In the cue, choose “Own address…” and type the address from its documentation, or catch it with the OSC monitor.",
"osc.howto.grandMA3": "1. On the console: Menu → In & Out → OSC.\n2. Add a line: Interface = the network port to the show network, Destination IP = this Mac's IP (below), Port = 8000, Prefix = gma3.\n3. Turn on Receive and Receive Command for the line, and Enable Input.\n4. Enter the console's IP here.",
"osc.howto.magicQ": "1. On the console: Setup → View Settings → Network.\n2. OSC Mode = OSC Rx (or Tx and Rx), OSC Rx Port = 8000.\n3. Enter the console's IP here (Setup → View Settings → Network shows it).",
"osc.howto.resolume": "1. In Resolume open Preferences → OSC.\n2. Turn on OSC Input; leave the port 7000 (or type the same port here).\n3. Same Mac: press “This Mac”. Another computer: enter its IP (on that Mac: System Settings → Network).",
"osc.howto.x32": "1. Nothing to switch on: the console always listens for OSC on port 10023.\n2. Enter the console's IP (on the console: Setup → Network).\n3. The console and this Mac must be on the same network.",
